{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01227",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.68,
      "end_seconds": 3.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "good morning. I've just opened your notes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 4.48,
      "end_seconds": 10.98,
      "duration_seconds": 6.5,
      "text": "Yeah, hello, doctor. I hope it's alright if I stay in for this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.01,
      "end_seconds": 15.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Start wherever you like, I'm listening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 17.99,
      "end_seconds": 22.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "we came because of an itchy patch on my wrist"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.07,
      "end_seconds": 27.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.69,
      "end_seconds": 36.18,
      "duration_seconds": 7.49,
      "text": "Mm, it's a... um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a little pink tablet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.57,
      "end_seconds": 40.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "So, do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 41.92,
      "end_seconds": 64.3,
      "duration_seconds": 22.38,
      "text": "For the fluid, I believe. My husband sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given. It's Glycomet, 500 milligrams, twice a day. It's apixaban, 5 milligrams, twice a day for the heart rhythm. A plain moisturiser. I take it twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.03,
      "end_seconds": 68.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "When did you start it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.66,
      "end_seconds": 70.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "About about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.52,
      "end_seconds": 75.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "okay, how long has this been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.65,
      "end_seconds": 84.29,
      "duration_seconds": 7.64,
      "text": "It's been six months now. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.31,
      "end_seconds": 88.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Is anything making it worse?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.9,
      "end_seconds": 93.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "It's worse with my new watch strap."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.34,
      "end_seconds": 96.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "How often do you get it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.22,
      "end_seconds": 102.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "Mm, it sort of comes and goes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.72,
      "end_seconds": 110.93,
      "duration_seconds": 7.21,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 111.03,
      "end_seconds": 115.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.78,
      "end_seconds": 121.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "Hmm, I was getting to that!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.33,
      "end_seconds": 128.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "Okay, that's fine, one at a time. I'll ask about everything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.22,
      "end_seconds": 134.3,
      "duration_seconds": 5.08,
      "text": "and there's a bit of redness as well, two months now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.3,
      "end_seconds": 138.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "A few quick ones: spreading or blisters?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.98,
      "end_seconds": 152.27,
      "duration_seconds": 13.29,
      "text": "Um, no, no spreading, no blisters. I did have dry flaky skin at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.22,
      "end_seconds": 154.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "any sign of fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.84,
      "end_seconds": 158.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "definitely no fever"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 160.05,
      "end_seconds": 165.59,
      "duration_seconds": 5.54,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice fever. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.27,
      "end_seconds": 173.27,
      "duration_seconds": 7.0,
      "text": "no, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.42,
      "end_seconds": 184.72,
      "duration_seconds": 7.3,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Any trouble with the waterworks?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.05,
      "end_seconds": 189.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "mm, uh, no, that's all fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.54,
      "end_seconds": 199.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Anything with your heart, like skipped beats or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.5,
      "end_seconds": 203.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "No, nothing with my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.95,
      "end_seconds": 209.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "so, has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 210.57,
      "end_seconds": 217.44,
      "duration_seconds": 6.87,
      "text": "Yeah, I've had heart failure, yes. Right, I have diabetes, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.28,
      "end_seconds": 219.25,
      "duration_seconds": 0.97,
      "text": "Right, right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 220.28,
      "end_seconds": 224.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "I have an irregular heartbeat, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.32,
      "end_seconds": 238.12,
      "duration_seconds": 11.8,
      "text": "Yes. Right, so heart failure and diabetes are already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. Do you follow any particular diet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 239.42,
      "end_seconds": 242.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "I'm vegetarian and have been for years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.43,
      "end_seconds": 245.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.07,
      "end_seconds": 250.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.11,
      "end_seconds": 254.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 256.16,
      "end_seconds": 257.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.02,
      "text": "No, never."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.8,
      "end_seconds": 262.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 263.73,
      "end_seconds": 269.45,
      "duration_seconds": 5.72,
      "text": "sorry, what was I saying, yes, naproxen. I get stomach pain"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.58,
      "end_seconds": 285.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 286.23,
      "end_seconds": 290.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Ah, my mother has an underactive thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.11,
      "end_seconds": 293.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "May I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.03,
      "end_seconds": 296.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "look straight ahead"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.65,
      "end_seconds": 311.26,
      "duration_seconds": 5.61,
      "text": "there's a neat red patch where the watch strap sits, with a little scaling"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 328.2,
      "end_seconds": 329.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.05,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 334.72,
      "end_seconds": 368.86,
      "duration_seconds": 34.14,
      "text": "Alright, you can sit up now. Taking everything into account, the most likely explanation is mild contact dermatitis from the watch strap. Eczema is also on my list. Let's use hydrocortisone cream, 1%, once a day, one week. It's for contact dermatitis. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well. Stop wearing that strap and and keep the skin moisturised. Book a review if it has not cleared in two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 370.03,
      "end_seconds": 373.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Come by reception afterwards and I'll fix the appointment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 375.3,
      "end_seconds": 378.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 383.24,
      "end_seconds": 387.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.73,
      "text": "Mm, uh, I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 391.63,
      "end_seconds": 393.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "have a good day"
    }
  ]
}